Unless a file or notice states otherwise:

1. Original narrative text, chapters, website prose, documentation, and
   original figures are licensed under Creative Commons Attribution 4.0
   International (CC BY 4.0). See LICENSES/CC-BY-4.0.txt.

2. Original code embedded in released chapters, together with Python,
   workflow, configuration, and website code, is licensed under the MIT
   License. See LICENSES/MIT.txt.

3. Release 2026.1 distributes no standalone dataset. If a QMSBR-generated
   synthetic dataset is separately published in a later release, it will be
   dedicated under Creative Commons CC0 1.0 Universal unless that release says
   otherwise. See LICENSES/CC0-1.0.txt.

4. Examples in the released chapters use a curated subset derived from the UCI
   Student Performance dataset. The dataset is not distributed in Release
   2026.1; its upstream CC BY 4.0 terms and attribution remain applicable. See
   NOTICE.

5. The Citation Style Language style used as a private render dependency is not
   deployed. It retains CC BY-SA 3.0 and its upstream attribution. See
   LICENSES/CC-BY-SA-3.0.txt and NOTICE.

6. Package datasets, generated framework assets, cited publications, names,
   and trademarks retain their upstream terms. See NOTICE. No rights are
   granted beyond those held by the QMSBR copyright holder.

Attribution for CC BY material should identify Jinsong Chen, name QMSBR,
identify the release and its public source URL once assigned, and indicate
whether changes were made.
